<!--T:1-->
{{SITENAME}} turns a directory of wikitext files into a static website. It runs MediaWiki itself, so pages are written with the markup, templates and parser functions a wiki gives you, and then captures the result: what it writes out is plain HTML, CSS, JavaScript and images, served by anything that serves files. There is no server and no database behind the published site.

<!--T:2-->
This site is one of its builds. Every page here comes from a <code>.wikitext</code> file under [<tvar name="1">https://github.com/chaotic-ground/wikven/tree/main/docs</tvar> <code>docs/</code>], baked by the same [<tvar name="2">https://github.com/chaotic-ground/wikven/tree/main/actions/bake</tvar> action] the documentation recommends, and the "Edit" and "View history" links on each page lead to that file in the repository.

